                <pb facs="0521" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg514"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94111/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-06T17:00:00-04:00">September 6, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>218. Department’s 152, August 16, 2 p.m., and your 461, August 18, 1 p.m. Please
                    review this matter in the light of the situation as it now exists and give me by
                    priority radio the benefit of your further views and any comments you may have
                    to offer on the advisability of putting into effect at this stage the initial
                    provision or more of the Act under reference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
